WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Inheritor of Courage</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.810
<b>Yokosuka Special Economic Zone</b>

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.410
Alma!

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.480
Minami!

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.540
Alma!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.100
An unknown model... 
There's absolutely no intel on it!

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.150
Is <i>that</i> the extra gear?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.160
<b>Counter EX-ARM HQ</b>

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.160
Chief, what is that?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:57.670
<i>A cutting-edge SA-class combat exoframe 
designed by Iriya Heavy Industries.</i>

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.230
<i>Ignis Type 02X:</i>

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.760
<i>Ogre.</i>

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.730
We made it? I've heard nothing about this!

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:17.700
<i>It was the CEO's secret pet project.</i>

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:20.890
God, that woman drives me up the wall.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:25.210
And who's controlling this SA-class exoframe?

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:25.860
It can't be...

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.130
Akira?!

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.860
It is. I'm seeing an enormous spike 
in traffic.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.650
How was he able to get it 
moving like that within seconds?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.630
Normally, we'd need 
the Prime Minister's approval to deploy it,

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.430
but that's not a problem in the SEZ.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:50.810
<i>And</i> I got the green light for six hours 
of unrestricted firearm use.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.000
I can tell how to move this thing.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.300
How to run, jump, and even fire a gun.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:31.480
It's almost as if I've done this 
countless times before.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.890
Anything that gets in our way 
must be eliminated. <i>Anything.</i>

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.080
Kondo, is that who I think it is?

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.740
Yeah. I'm being told it's Akira.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.350
It's an Iriya prototype and our shiny new toy.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.240
I can't believe a damn box 
can fight like that.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.040
Major Whitman! You need to see this!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.580
Why does a police force have such powerful weaponry? 
Who do they think they are?!

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.540
<b>UN Military Base</b>

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.010
We can't let them act like they own our turf!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.360
Patch me through to the States. 
No more Mr. Nice Guy!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.260
Yes, sir!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.340
It's me, Minami! Can you hear me?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.600
I can hold Elmira off with this thing.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.890
I'll buy you some time to rescue 
and evacuate the civilians.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.600
Gotcha!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.350
I'll help.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.200
Don't force it, Alma.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.820
I'm fine. I don't feel any pain.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:29.420
Also, my arm isn't completely gone. 
It's just somewhere else.

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.030
Damn it!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.560
My bullets can't penetrate 
that thick-ass armor!

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.620
Is there no way to take down that Bibot?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.510
Found it.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:43.790
Alma's missing arm.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.760
The piece of the bodysuit 
attached to it sent an SOS.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.930
Yeah, I knew it wasn't scientifically possible 
to just make things go away.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:50.840
So where is it?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.410
In the Tokyo Bay waters? Why?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.720
Send in a drone from MPD! Now!

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.200
This way!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.200
Are you okay?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.670
Thank you.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.070
<b>Skies over the MPD</b>

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.860
It'll get to the point soon.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.300
Switching to visual data.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.500
<b>Tokyo Bay</b>

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.080
What is that?

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.430
Something just got dumped 
into the water from mid-air.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.300
What the...

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:34.460
Would you look at that! 
I think I know how that ability works now!

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.600
<b>Yokosuka SEZ</b>

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.600
<b>UN Military Base</b>

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.200
Excuse me?

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.600
It swaps entire spaces?!

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.680
Yeah.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:31.570
That EX-ARM doesn't vaporize its targets. 
It just sends them someplace else!

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.540
Whatever it "destroys" just gets dumped 
in another location.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.750
So, if we fire a missile 
at its dumping portal...

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.610
I'm good to go.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:52.210
Great. Just think of it as playing a game.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.800
You picked the right woman to do this, then!

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.930
Lock on to the coordinates.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:00.970
Copy that.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.850
Okay, here's the plan.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:09.340
Akira, attack Elmira at close range 
and force her to deploy her portal.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:12.860
We'll launch a bomb at that portal

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.530
and send it flying into Elmira's face.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.200
Got it!

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.140
There she is!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.480
Akira!

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.380
Akira...

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.430
Akira.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.830
I got this.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.130
Damn, he tamed the hounds!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:39.010
Go!

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.140
Did he hack them?!

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.070
Now, Chikage!

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.250
Shoot the missile into the portal!

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.160
Firing now!

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:08.260
Hit the target!

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:12.710
Sweet!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.200
Did we get her?!

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.340
Wait. Look!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.530
I'm terribly sorry, Master Mraw.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.930
Please don't worry so.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:34.620
I'm not out of it yet.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:37.360
The hell is up with that?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.950
Please don't tell me that's Mraw.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.150
I hate to break it to you, but it is.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.130
He's still alive, but in a vegetative state.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.940
He's probably brain dead.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.970
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:07.100
Wait. How is his EX-ARM still functioning, then?

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:11.180
I found Elmira's spec data.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:15.480
It seems Mraw embedded 
an illegal data-sharing device in his brain.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.860
A brain implant? So that's it!

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:27.830
A VR system that's installed directly in the brain 
and enables data sharing!

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:34.660
Mraw connected to Elmira 
using dangerous, unapproved technology.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:42.430
I shall switch to emergency mode, Master Mraw.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.710
Emergency mode activated.

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.790
It's the same thing as the priest!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:52.410
The EX-ARM will stop functioning 
if its user dies!

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.740
Shoot Mraw dead,

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.510
Akira!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.010
No point firing randomly.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.410
It's swapping the spaces out 
at insane speed.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.930
Fire another bomb, then! Chikage!

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:10.860
I can't.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:14.230
I don't see a thing. I'm pretty sure 
I locked on to the coordinates, too.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.210
Looks like the portal was moved.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:22.470
There's no way we can find 
the new coordinates immediately.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:28.640
There's no fooling me twice.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:33.810
Oh shit! We're in danger here!

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:37.960
Guys!

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:41.230
Please stop this, Elmira!

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:42.670
Akira!

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.170
Minami? You okay?!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:48.650
Yeah, just barely. But Kondo's...

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.980
I screwed up. My bad.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.110
Her swapping's getting more frequent 
by the second.

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:58.130
I've got my hands full 
just dodging her attacks.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.710
Elmira's swapping range is starting to expand!

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.880
How is she covering so much space?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.340
It's gotta be GPS!

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.400
Hello?

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.640
The UN is what?!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.890
<i>HQ to all agents.</i>

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.080
<i>The UN Military sent word to the MPD.</i>

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:20.220
<i>They're going to use a fuel-air explosive.</i>

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:21.180
What?!

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.530
The bomber's headed your way as we speak.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.760
Mraw's Bibot is now within a kilo 
of the base!

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.070
The general gave us the okay.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:35.620
We've been ordered to prevent its escape, 
even if we gotta burn the damn city down!

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:37.840
Is this the end of the line?

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:40.710
The bomber's almost at Yokosuka.

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:44.490
They can't be serious. 
The whole city's gonna blow!

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.720
<i>Hurry up and get out of there!</i>

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:54.000
<i>Come in, Akira! You have to retreat!</i>

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.100
<i>This is an order!</i>

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:58.230
The bomb hasn't been dropped yet.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.380
Let me keep at it as long as I can!

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:06.950
I know there's gotta be something I can do! 
I'm putting my best foot forward!

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.360
Damn it!

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.910
Wake up, Elmira! Mraw's dead!

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:21.500
His vitals are still alive.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.750
He asked me to protect his life.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.970
And that order is my top priority.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:33.390
I will obey any order he gives me. 
That is my very purpose.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:39.240
Nothing you do will make him happy anymore!

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:44.320
So long as his order still stands, 
I will obey and uphold it.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:48.860
That will bring him happiness, 
and his happiness is my happiness.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.780
How are you any different?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.290
Your happiness lies in constant battle.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:04.000
Is that not why you were built as an EX-ARM?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:30.860
That's what we were built for...

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:36.540
To destroy it all.

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:46.540
Wrong.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:52.470
I absolutely will not let it happen.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:55.720
I will use my everything

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:01.020
to stop you here and now.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:08.570
So fast!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.710
What's happening?!

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.380
That punk removed all the restrictions 
placed on him!

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.710
His brain temp's crossed critical!

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.290
Telemetry monitoring's stopped working!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.170
All the safety fallbacks have been deactivated!

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.130
Akira's brain can't take this!

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.580
Akira!

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:30.520
Come in, Akira!

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.220
<i>Akira!</i>

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:46.570
Akira?

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.110
What is he, some kinda monster?

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:52.860
That noise...

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:54.400
No!

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.650
<i>Visual on target.</i>

00:16:56.650 --> 00:16:58.330
<i>Entering bombing trajectory.</i>

00:16:58.330 --> 00:16:59.780
<i>We are a go.</i>

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:03.050
Oh, god...

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.160
It's too late.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.170
Akira!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.770
<b>not so fast</b>

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.770
Not so fast.

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.560
The drop switch ain't responding!

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.110
Plane's going out of control!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.410
We're being hacked.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.140
Someone took over the system!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.870
We can't drop the BLU!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:47.370
No. Nobody could ever break in
 to our network!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:53.660
Even the higher privileges 
are being taken over!

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.680
What?!

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:56.630
It's... It's trying to...

00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:00.050
You're done, Elmira.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.050
<b>it's over</b>

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.050
<b>Elmira</b>

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.600
Is he charging in head-on?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.310
What's wrong with him?

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.510
Target locked on.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.680
GPS coordinates acquired. Converted.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:13.240
Predicting trajectory. 
Accounting for margin of error.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:14.480
Transmitting data.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.110
You're the one who's done for!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.150
Master Mraw!

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:39.750
He did it?

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.570
Akira...

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:44.650
Akira!

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.430
How did he do that?

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:55.130
Akira... What the hell have you done?

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:57.190
What happened, Professor?

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.740
He altered her target.

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:07.620
I said Elmira chooses her target coordinates 
using GPS, remember?

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:13.560
And you know what Akira did?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:20.130
He used the UN's armored vehicle's data link, 
accessed the military network,

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:25.640
<b>NORAD: North American 
Aerospace Defense Command</b>

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:25.300
broke into NORAD's systems, 
which operate the GPS satellites,

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:30.850
and moved the satellites up in space!

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.790
He did what?!

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:34.270
Wait a second!

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.680
Even the slightest deviation in GPS signals 
could be catastrophic!

00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:40.320
Too late.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.570
Things are going crazy all over the world.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:47.850
Forgive me, Master Mraw.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:52.080
I appear to have... erred.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.650
No!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:00.270
All she was doing was following orders!

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:02.170
It's not all her fault!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.670
Didn't you want to go back to being human?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:13.350
Come back to your senses first, you moron!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.610
Akira.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.560
Let me take you back.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:41.660
Akira!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.640
The link got shut down due to overload.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:49.100
Looks like the safety functions came back online.

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:51.770
<i>Don't talk about him like that!</i>

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:55.180
Akira's human, and you know it!

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:28.560
Hold up, Superintendent! 
What's with this outfit?

00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:31.720
Wear it for him. 
Also, it actually looks good on you.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.480
N-Not happy to hear it!

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.570
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 005 - Red-Hot Daydream."

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Red-Hot Daydream!</b>

00:23:36.570 --> 00:23:39.290
This will be the first and last time!
